      "overheat_basis": "ev"
    },
    "peg": {
      "_comment": "Flywheel rule (review applied 2026-10-28). Turns ON only on a completed daily CLOSE >= on_close_threshold for that preferred (STRC $100.00, SATA $99.80); an intraday touch never turns it on, and before the 4 PM ET close the call uses the last completed close. Once ON it stays ON until it trades below on_trade_threshold for MORE THAN off_minutes_below consecutive regular-session minutes (overnight/weekend gaps don't count). Labels: RUNNING_HOT (on, price >= running_hot.price_min AND heavy volume) > ON ('FLYWHEEL ON') > WARMING_UP (OFF for the call / watch only: traded >= on_trade_threshold without a qualifying close; STRC closes $99.80-$99.99 too) > COOLING_OFF (off, price >= stalled_below) > STALLED (off, below stalled_below). Older history with daily bars only: ON at a qualifying close; OFF at a close < on_trade_threshold; a day whose high touched on_trade_threshold but closed below the close threshold is WARMING_UP (off). full_on_threshold is now display-only (share of closes at/above it). See scripts/flywheel.py.",
